CUBE(1)                        P32W Unix                         CUBE(1)

NAME
       cube - a cube of twelve lines, turning

SYNOPSIS
       cube [frames]

DESCRIPTION
       cube draws a cube as its twelve edges and turns it: five
       degrees about its upright axis in every frame, and tipped
       half as fast about the axis from side to side, so that 72
       frames are one whole turn. Under the window manager
       (wm(1)) it has a window of its own, 240 dots square, which
       its corner makes bigger or smaller; with no window manager
       it takes the whole of the video card's screen (video(4)).

       It turns until q is typed (with its window in front, under
       wm), or its window's box is clicked, or for the number of
       frames given. With a number it does not wait between
       frames, and says at the end how long they took: the
       machine's speed at lines in three dimensions.

       It is P8X's cube brought to this machine, and the first
       program of g3d(3).

EXAMPLES
       cube
       win cube
       cube 72
              one turn, timed

       It is on the finder's Apps menu.

FILES
       /usr/src/cmd/cube.c        its source
       /usr/include/g3d.h         the library it is drawn with

SEE ALSO
       house(1), g3d(3), gfx(3), wm(1), win(1)
